WEBVTT

00:08.690 --> 00:16.160
aozameta machinami yureru boku no kage

00:08.690 --> 00:16.160
The pale street, my swaying shadow,

00:16.160 --> 00:24.440
nibui ashidori wa yuku saki wo shirazu

00:16.160 --> 00:24.440
I walk slowly, not knowing my destination.

00:24.440 --> 00:30.480
kawasenu omoi

00:24.440 --> 00:30.480
My feelings can't reach yours.

00:31.240 --> 00:38.620
kimi no hitomi no naka utsushidasu mono wo

00:31.240 --> 00:38.620
The things reflected in the depths of your eyes,

00:38.620 --> 00:46.860
uketomeru tame ni hashiridashiteita

00:38.620 --> 00:46.860
I started running in order to catch up to them.

00:46.860 --> 01:00.640
sashidasu sono te wo hodokerai youni nigirikaesu

00:46.860 --> 01:00.640
I grip your outstretched hand without letting go.

01:01.170 --> 01:08.680
hanbun no tsuki no yoru wa bokura wo terashite

01:01.170 --> 01:08.680
On this night, the half moon shines upon us.

01:08.680 --> 01:15.990
oikaketekita jikan wo boku wa furikitte

01:08.680 --> 01:15.990
I shake off the flow of time chasing after us.

01:16.220 --> 01:27.430
hanbun zutsu no bokura wa egaku saki made mo mieru

01:16.220 --> 01:27.430
We're half of ourselves, but we can draw the future.

01:34.040 --> 01:39.430
Note: Welcome to Ise

01:46.120 --> 01:47.350
Ise Udon

01:46.450 --> 01:47.350
Oh crap.

01:53.860 --> 01:57.600
Wakaba Municipal Hospital

01:57.800 --> 01:59.920
Note: Night Entrance

02:14.880 --> 02:17.880
Note: Nurse Station

02:30.160 --> 02:31.630
Yuuichi!

02:30.160 --> 02:31.630
Ah, Akiko-san! It's not like that!

02:31.630 --> 02:33.260
I just went to the washroom for a bit!

02:36.430 --> 02:39.940
Ezaki Yuuichi

02:36.700 --> 02:39.940
Akiko-san, the Girl and Akutagawa Ryuunosuke

02:40.240 --> 02:41.670
You know, Yuuichi.

02:41.670 --> 02:44.130
How many times do I have to say this until you understand?

02:45.210 --> 02:46.310
Honestly...

02:46.310 --> 02:48.530
I only went out for a walk...

02:50.150 --> 02:52.720
You sneak off right after the lights go out, right?

02:52.720 --> 02:54.550
It's not like that!

02:54.550 --> 02:55.790
I fell asleep immediately.

02:55.790 --> 02:57.910
Falling asleep is true...

02:58.960 --> 03:01.390
But it's only your bag!

03:02.190 --> 03:05.730
Don't go out on your own authority just because you feel slightly better!

03:06.060 --> 03:08.030
Be careful or you'll never get out of the hospital!

03:08.030 --> 03:09.270
Do you understand?

03:09.270 --> 03:10.050
Hey!

03:10.570 --> 03:13.890
The next time I catch you sneaking off, I'll make you dance naked in public.

03:14.470 --> 03:15.710
You don't want to, right?

03:15.710 --> 03:17.640
That'd be regretful, right?

03:17.640 --> 03:19.680
Or, do you want to dance like that?

03:19.680 --> 03:22.280
No, I don't want to...

03:22.280 --> 03:25.020
Then obey my command like a good boy.

03:25.020 --> 03:27.620
There are girls living in this hospital too.

03:27.620 --> 03:29.950
It'll be really embarrassing for you if they see you like that.

03:29.950 --> 03:31.210
Girls?

03:34.860 --> 03:36.860
Hey! You touched my ass, didn't you?

03:37.360 --> 03:39.400
I'm sorry, Akiko-chan.

03:39.730 --> 03:42.870
This hallway is too narrow, I touched it by accident.

03:42.870 --> 03:45.570
You perverted old man! Don't lie!

03:45.570 --> 03:51.240
How could you suspect a sickly, weak grandfather like me?

03:51.240 --> 03:54.150
What a cruel child.

03:56.180 --> 03:59.050
Don't pretend to be sick only at times like this.

03:59.050 --> 04:01.650
My heart is pumping so hard.

04:01.650 --> 04:02.720
My blood pressure too...

04:02.720 --> 04:04.760
Stop lying and die, old man.

04:06.190 --> 04:08.680
What's the matter with that? It's just dancing naked.

04:09.130 --> 04:12.760
Tsukasa, you can joke about it since you don't know the true Akiko-san.

04:12.760 --> 04:16.100
Note: Ise Gulf Coast Motocycle Gang

04:13.830 --> 04:16.100
Bring it on!

04:16.630 --> 04:19.690
She will do what she said. That's the scary part.

04:20.070 --> 04:23.540
You'll get a cold if you dance naked in the winter.

04:23.980 --> 04:29.380
Besides, your hepatitis is supposed to be like a cold in the first place.

04:29.380 --> 04:32.720
It'll get better by itself if you just sleep for a few days, so dancing a bit won't matter.

04:32.720 --> 04:35.420
Hearing it from your mouth makes me a bit angry.

04:35.420 --> 04:36.450
And...

04:36.450 --> 04:39.090
Those manjuu are supposed to be for me!

04:36.490 --> 04:40.390
Note: Manjuu is a steamed bun-like cake, popular and traditional Japanese confections.

04:39.090 --> 04:40.390
Don't eat them all by yourself!

04:40.390 --> 04:41.630
Do you want to have some?

04:42.260 --> 04:43.230
But...

04:43.230 --> 04:45.420
What Yamanishi said is true.

04:46.000 --> 04:49.450
My illness only requires 2-3 months of rest and it'll be cured.

04:50.370 --> 04:52.420
The name of the illness is Hepatitis A,

04:52.970 --> 04:54.970
which looks like a cold on the surface.

04:54.970 --> 04:57.830
I've been admitted into the hospital for about a month and my condition has improved a lot.

04:58.140 --> 05:00.650
But there's really nothing to do here, so I'm going crazy out of boredom.

05:04.520 --> 05:06.120
Tanaka-sensei from the Internal Medicine Department.

05:08.120 --> 05:10.620
Please come to the nurse station immidiately.

05:11.220 --> 05:11.860
Ouch!

05:12.220 --> 05:13.690
Sorry, sorry...

05:13.690 --> 05:15.090
I'll do it again.

05:15.090 --> 05:16.530
No skill.

05:16.530 --> 05:18.330
3 days ago,

05:18.330 --> 05:20.870
somebody transferred from a hospital outside of the province.

05:21.430 --> 05:22.900
Akiba Rika-chan,

05:23.270 --> 05:25.670
17 years old, just like you.

05:26.870 --> 05:28.140
Are you interested?

05:28.140 --> 05:30.140
It's not like that.

05:30.140 --> 05:31.080
But...

05:31.080 --> 05:33.380
If she's living in the East Wing...

05:33.380 --> 05:34.970
Is her condition that serious?

05:35.580 --> 05:36.350
Well...

05:36.350 --> 05:37.670
Never mind.

05:48.330 --> 05:50.960
What are you doing, Akiko-san?

05:50.960 --> 05:52.730
Can't you tell by looking?

05:52.730 --> 05:55.870
The emergency procedure to prevent you from sneaking off.

05:55.870 --> 05:58.840
No way! What if I wanted to go to the washroom?

05:59.140 --> 05:59.820
Here.

06:01.670 --> 06:03.030
A-Are you serious?

06:03.570 --> 06:04.680
I'm serious.

06:05.080 --> 06:06.500
Take care.

06:11.920 --> 06:14.620
Illusion!

06:14.620 --> 06:18.220
So, today's program, Hiroshirai Yoshikazu's Happy Cooking Time, is about to start.

06:18.220 --> 06:20.660
Look at this, this is the key.

06:21.190 --> 06:27.170
Would the staff members, who are participating in today's 5 o'clock fire drill, please meet outside the reception area.

06:30.370 --> 06:34.370
Note: Akiba Rika

06:38.340 --> 06:39.700
Hello!

06:55.960 --> 06:57.300
Ah, how nice...

06:57.300 --> 06:58.400
This is the best.

06:58.800 --> 06:59.830
Smoke?

06:59.830 --> 07:02.130
Then, I'll have some.

07:03.500 --> 07:04.790
Ouch!

07:05.440 --> 07:06.840
Idiot.

07:06.840 --> 07:09.840
What are you so worked up for. You're underage, right?

07:09.840 --> 07:13.260
If you can't even take this little temptation, what'll you do?

07:16.810 --> 07:18.020
Feels good.

07:18.020 --> 07:20.080
I'll have my revenge one day.

07:21.450 --> 07:23.370
This sure is a small town.

07:23.720 --> 07:25.090
Yeah.

07:25.320 --> 07:28.050
What are you planning to do after you graduate from high school?

07:28.660 --> 07:31.920
I want to go to university, either in Tokyo or Nagoya.

07:32.860 --> 07:34.890
You want to leave this town?

07:35.400 --> 07:36.790
That's what I'm thinking.

07:38.770 --> 07:40.560
I envy you.

07:41.970 --> 07:44.910
Why don't you leave then?

07:44.910 --> 07:47.450
Well, saying it is one thing...

07:47.850 --> 07:50.270
But to actually do it is harder than you think.

07:54.750 --> 07:56.120
Aside from that,

07:56.120 --> 07:57.990
that bench...

07:57.990 --> 07:59.520
How about I take it away?

07:59.520 --> 08:00.690
Can you?

08:00.690 --> 08:02.090
I guess.

08:02.090 --> 08:04.400
But there's one condition.

08:04.800 --> 08:05.700
Condition?

08:05.700 --> 08:06.630
Yeah.

08:07.470 --> 08:11.170
Can you go and keep Rika-chan company for a bit?

08:11.170 --> 08:12.640
Rika...

08:12.640 --> 08:13.990
You mean Akiba Rika?

08:14.370 --> 08:16.710
She might be a bit hard to talk to...

08:16.710 --> 08:18.710
Note: Akutagawa Ryuunosuke Complete Collection 1

08:17.140 --> 08:18.710
But she's a good kid.

08:20.210 --> 08:25.720
Note: Akutagawa Ryuunosuke was a Japanese poet and writer, regarded as the "Father of the Japanese short story".

08:20.610 --> 08:22.370
Akutagawa Ryuunosuke.

08:22.910 --> 08:24.540
She's one of his fans.

08:24.450 --> 08:25.720
Epic Play Collection

08:24.450 --> 08:25.720
Akutagawa Ryuunosuke
Complete Collection 1

08:25.720 --> 08:27.720
Akiba Rika

08:31.190 --> 08:35.180
I'll tell her that you like Akutagawa's book too.

08:39.700 --> 08:40.500
Who's there?

08:41.630 --> 08:42.950
Is someone there?

08:44.570 --> 08:47.310
That's the condition in exchange of me taking the bench away.

08:51.510 --> 08:53.060
G-Good day.

09:01.120 --> 09:03.790
Are you the person Tanizaki-san told me about?

09:03.790 --> 09:05.110
Tanizaki?

09:05.660 --> 09:08.460
Ah, you're talking about Akiko-san?

09:08.460 --> 09:10.480
I've already read that book.

09:13.230 --> 09:15.920
My favorite story is the one called "Mikan,"

09:13.230 --> 09:17.970
Note: "Mikan" (lit. orange) is a short story by Akutagawa Ryuunosuke.

09:16.230 --> 09:17.970
even though it's short and simple.

09:18.470 --> 09:19.860
But it's a nice story, isn't it?

09:23.540 --> 09:25.260
It's good, the oranges...

09:28.780 --> 09:31.350
Did you really read it?

09:41.490 --> 09:42.610
Well...

09:43.430 --> 09:45.260
This is your first time here, right?

09:45.260 --> 09:47.100
I heard from Akiko-san.

09:47.800 --> 09:50.030
It really is a country-side city with nothing in it...

09:50.030 --> 09:51.960
There's the Grand Shrine of Ise, though.

09:53.140 --> 09:54.530
Have you been there before?

10:00.310 --> 10:02.380
Since it's a small city,

10:02.380 --> 10:05.080
you can see the entire city through this window.

10:05.620 --> 10:07.850
The school I went to and the library too.

10:08.890 --> 10:13.860
Note: "Houdai" literally means "gun turret".

10:08.890 --> 10:12.220
My house is behind Mt. Houdai, so you can't see it.

10:12.690 --> 10:14.060
Mt. Houdai?

10:14.060 --> 10:15.330
Y-Yeah...

10:15.330 --> 10:18.360
I heard a long time ago, there was a gun turret on the mountain top.

10:18.700 --> 10:20.470
So everyone here started calling it like that.

10:22.700 --> 10:23.970
U-Umm...

10:24.470 --> 10:25.400
Sorry...

10:25.400 --> 10:28.170
Akiko-san said it'd be better to talk about common interests.

10:28.640 --> 10:32.940
And I didn't want to lie to you.

10:35.380 --> 10:36.810
I'll forgive you,

10:38.050 --> 10:40.690
because you've found what I was looking for.

10:42.920 --> 10:43.920
But...

10:44.760 --> 10:46.160
There's one condition.

10:51.530 --> 10:53.260
Note: Ise Municipal Library Hometown Book Collection

11:07.010 --> 11:08.480
What took you so long?

11:09.150 --> 11:10.350
Did you find the book?

11:10.950 --> 11:11.950
I found it.

11:15.820 --> 11:16.720
What's this?

11:16.720 --> 11:19.520
This isn't the one I wanted to read.

11:19.920 --> 11:23.090
Didn't I ask you not to borrow this one no matter what?

11:23.090 --> 11:24.500
I-Is that right?

11:25.400 --> 11:26.600
What an idiot!

11:26.600 --> 11:28.300
You can't even do a simple thing like this.

11:28.300 --> 11:29.530
How useless!

11:31.440 --> 11:32.900
I'm sorry.

11:32.900 --> 11:34.770
You can go again.

11:36.170 --> 11:38.810
It's really cold outside today.

11:39.310 --> 11:40.310
So...

11:40.950 --> 11:41.850
What's wrong?

11:43.050 --> 11:46.250
Didn't you say you'd do whatever I say?

11:46.250 --> 11:47.390
I got it.

11:47.720 --> 11:48.990
I'm going.

11:48.990 --> 11:50.020
You'd better hurry.

11:50.020 --> 11:51.760
The library is about to close.

11:53.290 --> 11:54.830
I'll hurry.

12:11.810 --> 12:13.540
You'll have to do...

12:13.540 --> 12:15.550
whatever I say...

12:15.880 --> 12:17.050
No matter what.

12:17.450 --> 12:21.190
If I say I want something, just bring it to me.

12:21.190 --> 12:23.190
If I say, "make me laugh,"

12:23.190 --> 12:25.560
do something funny that will make me laugh.

12:25.990 --> 12:29.060
Then, I'll forgive you.

12:29.060 --> 12:35.070
Akiba Rika

12:29.560 --> 12:30.900
I got the book.

12:31.230 --> 12:32.760
There's no way it can be wrong this time.

12:33.260 --> 12:35.070
Then... I'll put it over here.

12:51.320 --> 12:53.620
Where did you go again?

12:53.990 --> 12:55.150
Is it because of this?

12:55.150 --> 12:56.650
I went to see a friend.

12:56.650 --> 12:58.260
That won't do.

12:58.260 --> 13:02.330
When I was your age, I already had a bunch.

13:02.660 --> 13:03.830
For you.

13:05.360 --> 13:06.430
Want to take a look?

13:06.430 --> 13:12.600
The resulting collection of my hard work during the time I spent in this hospital...

13:12.600 --> 13:14.510
Maybe next time...

13:23.050 --> 13:24.350
What do you think you're doing?

13:30.050 --> 13:32.290
Akutagawa Ryuunosuke
Complete Collection 1

13:38.160 --> 13:39.660
Hey...

13:39.660 --> 13:40.970
Come and keep me company.

13:45.470 --> 13:48.470
So this is what the operating room looks like.

13:48.470 --> 13:49.170
This is bad...

13:49.170 --> 13:50.680
We'll get scolded.

13:50.680 --> 13:52.380
Yuuichi, lay here for a bit.

13:54.180 --> 13:56.410
Well then, let's start the operation.

13:56.410 --> 13:57.680
Wait a second...

13:57.680 --> 13:58.680
What are you holding?

13:58.680 --> 13:59.820
A scalpel.

14:00.150 --> 14:02.250
Trust me, don't worry.

14:02.250 --> 14:03.090
Don't worry?

14:03.090 --> 14:04.160
How?

14:04.160 --> 14:05.820
What's not to worry about?

14:06.860 --> 14:08.360
Alright, let's start.

14:09.130 --> 14:10.400
Wa... Wai... Wait...

14:10.400 --> 14:11.660
Who's in there?

14:20.540 --> 14:21.670
Eh?

14:21.670 --> 14:24.640
I'm sure I heard voices in here.

14:32.450 --> 14:34.250
Yuuichi, you were so funny.

14:34.250 --> 14:36.390
Your face looked like you were having a stroke.

14:36.390 --> 14:38.890
If we were discovered, we'd have been killed for sure.

14:45.800 --> 14:46.900
Hey...

14:46.900 --> 14:48.570
Why didn't you ask me?

14:48.570 --> 14:49.430
Huh?

14:49.430 --> 14:50.740
Ask what?

14:51.270 --> 14:53.300
What's wrong with me.

14:57.380 --> 15:01.750
I heard everyone living in the East Wing are critical patients.

15:03.010 --> 15:04.620
As I thought, it's serious?

15:06.720 --> 15:07.850
I'll...

15:08.420 --> 15:09.820
probably die soon.

15:10.920 --> 15:13.560
Do you know the valves of the heart?

15:14.090 --> 15:15.890
The valves in my heart don't work well.

15:16.860 --> 15:18.800
There's no other option besides a transplant.

15:19.260 --> 15:21.430
But my body is really weak...

15:21.430 --> 15:24.240
The possibility of a failed operation is high.

15:25.300 --> 15:27.910
Papa went through the same operation for the same problem.

15:28.810 --> 15:30.680
During the operation,

15:30.680 --> 15:32.480
his heart stopped.

15:34.550 --> 15:36.210
If I want to proceed with the operation...

15:36.580 --> 15:39.050
Then I'll have to make the realization like Papa.

15:39.980 --> 15:41.290
Realization?

15:41.750 --> 15:44.060
Yuuichi, you said it before, right?

15:44.960 --> 15:47.690
That mountain is called Mt. Houdai.

15:48.830 --> 15:50.530
Before Papa had his operation,

15:50.530 --> 15:53.160
he brought me along when he climbed that mountain.

15:54.030 --> 15:57.740
He forced himself to bring me there,

15:57.740 --> 15:59.700
even though he was told that he couldn't climb.

16:00.300 --> 16:02.640
I think he made his realization at that time.

16:04.180 --> 16:08.010
I was really small then, so I don't remember where I was...

16:08.010 --> 16:11.320
But Papa said that it was Mt. Houdai.

16:11.680 --> 16:14.490
That's why you're always looking out the window.

16:16.050 --> 16:17.660
You're looking at the mountain.

16:18.820 --> 16:21.830
I really want to go there again.

16:22.530 --> 16:23.530
If I do that,

16:24.000 --> 16:26.330
maybe I can have my realization too.

16:37.910 --> 16:39.540
Ah, I'm dead...

16:41.080 --> 16:43.050
It's almost morning already.

16:43.410 --> 16:44.420
Are you going back?

16:45.150 --> 16:46.680
Later, Tsukasa.

16:51.060 --> 16:51.820
Hey,

16:51.820 --> 16:53.220
trouble kid.

16:54.130 --> 16:55.190
Tada-san...

16:55.190 --> 16:56.390
Did something happen?

16:57.160 --> 16:59.160
His condition suddenly deteriorated...

17:00.370 --> 17:01.630
He passed away...

17:03.700 --> 17:06.600
He has something for you.

17:13.540 --> 17:17.220
Tada-san recovered his consciousness once...

17:17.650 --> 17:20.350
I asked him if there was anything he wanted to say...

17:20.350 --> 17:23.550
He wanted to leave all these adult books to you...

17:24.520 --> 17:26.060
That was his only will.

17:26.560 --> 17:27.530
That's why...

17:27.530 --> 17:29.560
You should accept them graciously.

17:43.370 --> 17:44.080
Tsukasa...

17:49.610 --> 17:50.650
Wha...

17:50.650 --> 17:51.720
What do you want?

17:56.490 --> 17:57.360
Umm...

18:00.460 --> 18:01.230
Let's go.

18:03.830 --> 18:04.930
10 years ago...

18:05.300 --> 18:07.300
Your father took you there, right?

18:09.470 --> 18:11.540
This time, I'll take you there.

18:16.810 --> 18:17.710
Let's go.

18:18.040 --> 18:20.210
Take me there, Yuuichi.

18:32.390 --> 18:33.730
You two!

18:33.730 --> 18:35.160
What are you doing?!

18:35.160 --> 18:36.060
Hey, wait a second...

18:36.060 --> 18:37.560
Yuuichi!

18:40.930 --> 18:42.270
Zebra Mask?!

18:43.030 --> 18:43.770
Who's he?

18:44.840 --> 18:46.200
He's with us.

18:46.200 --> 18:47.870
Take this!

18:52.280 --> 18:55.180
Yuuichi, don't worry about me. Go!

18:56.180 --> 18:56.950
Let's go!

18:58.150 --> 18:59.880
Wait a second, Yuuichi!

18:59.880 --> 19:02.750
Don't you know what'll happen when you come back?

19:02.750 --> 19:04.890
Note: Night Entrance

19:05.420 --> 19:07.030
Tsukasa thought of everything.

19:50.640 --> 19:52.140
Here's the mountain top.

19:56.040 --> 19:58.510
I remember this place.

19:59.210 --> 20:02.510
I climbed up here with Papa's help.

20:34.450 --> 20:35.650
It's so pretty.

20:35.980 --> 20:37.550
Y-Yeah...

20:38.220 --> 20:39.250
It is.

20:40.450 --> 20:41.450
Yuuichi.

20:41.920 --> 20:42.790
Yes?

20:43.990 --> 20:45.020
Thank you.

20:46.060 --> 20:47.330
For what?

20:47.660 --> 20:49.030
I had my realization.

20:51.400 --> 20:52.800
My realization of death.

20:57.070 --> 21:00.340
Papa must've had this feeling at that time too.

21:05.040 --> 21:06.640
Papa also had his here...

21:28.870 --> 21:30.170
Hey, Yuuichi.

21:30.600 --> 21:32.600
Why are you doing so much for me?

21:33.770 --> 21:35.610
My father once said,

21:35.610 --> 21:37.840
"You have to cherish girls."

21:37.840 --> 21:39.510
Isn't that a good father?

21:40.040 --> 21:41.410
It's not like that.

21:41.750 --> 21:43.780
He always drank or gambled.

21:43.780 --> 21:44.880
He was the worst.

21:45.320 --> 21:46.250
Was?

21:46.850 --> 21:48.620
He died a long time ago.

21:49.050 --> 21:50.820
He broke his body from drinking.

21:53.360 --> 21:54.330
I see.

21:54.330 --> 21:56.260
That's why you brought me here.

21:56.590 --> 21:58.130
Yuuichi, you also...

21:58.130 --> 21:59.130
don't have a father.

21:59.130 --> 22:01.030
That's why you brought me here.

22:01.030 --> 22:01.770
Because we're the same...

22:01.770 --> 22:03.530
That's why you feel sympathy for me.

22:03.530 --> 22:06.570
No! It's not like that at all.

22:06.570 --> 22:08.640
This has no relation to my father.

22:09.140 --> 22:10.270
It's not like that...

22:10.270 --> 22:11.210
I...

22:12.110 --> 22:13.240
Yuuichi?

22:13.980 --> 22:16.250
I... I...

22:16.810 --> 22:17.750
Yuuichi!

22:19.650 --> 22:20.750
I...

22:21.150 --> 22:23.320
I... Rika...

22:38.600 --> 22:48.050
nee, yubisaki de anata wo kanjite

22:38.600 --> 22:48.050
Hey, I felt you with my fingers.

22:50.680 --> 23:00.190
nee, anata to miteita kono keshiki

22:50.680 --> 23:00.190
Hey, while seeing this view together.

23:03.730 --> 23:13.540
tsutawaru yasashisa ni mi wo yudanete

23:03.730 --> 23:13.540
And then I committed myself to your kindness.

23:13.540 --> 23:24.850
eien nado nai wakatte ita tsumori dayo

23:13.540 --> 23:24.850
I know nothing lasts forever.

23:28.090 --> 23:34.060
namae wo yobu anata no koe wo

23:28.090 --> 23:40.030
I will keep your voice, which calls my name, in the bottom of my heart,

23:34.060 --> 23:40.030
mune no oku ni shimatte oku kara

23:40.030 --> 23:46.140
hirakareta tobira no mukou gawa de

23:40.030 --> 23:46.140
On the other side of the open door,

23:46.140 --> 23:53.280
koborenu youni kienai youni

23:46.140 --> 23:53.280
That it won't overflow, it won't disappear.

24:01.590 --> 24:07.190
Next Episode

24:03.290 --> 24:04.420
It's a misunderstanding!

24:04.420 --> 24:05.560
At the same time, it's not a misunderstanding...

24:05.560 --> 24:07.330
There may not be any ill intent, but that's overdoing it a bit...

24:07.330 --> 24:08.990
Hey, they were inherited one way or another,

24:08.990 --> 24:10.760
so I can't just throw them away...

24:11.230 --> 24:13.670
I've finally gotten close with Rika...

24:13.670 --> 24:16.170
Why does everyone have to get in my way?

24:16.170 --> 24:19.300
And just who is this, this extra handsome man?

24:19.300 --> 24:22.270
Could he be Rika's ex-boyfriend?

24:23.010 --> 24:23.710
Next time:

24:23.710 --> 24:27.680
Looking up at the Half Moon:
Inheritance of the Tada Collection

24:25.610 --> 24:31.620
Inheritance of the Tada Collection

24:27.680 --> 24:28.750
It's my fault!

24:28.750 --> 24:30.520
Please, forgive me, Rika!
